-- The inline consensus fold — identity-routed, dedup-first, native.
--
-- NATIVE (2026-07-21, GH #565): the body lives in C (src/fold_route.c).
-- Consensus is content: dedup it the way ingest dedups laplace.entities. The batch is
-- split by what it IS, per relation type, then one MERGE handles matched and novel
-- cells against the literal-routed relation partition. Existing cells re-fold from
-- stored state; novel cells fold from the neutral prior.
--
-- History of the SQL forms this replaces (all measured, kept so nobody
-- re-tries them):
--  * Runtime-key MERGE: fanned out across ALL consensus leaves because type_id
--    arrived from the join (2026-07-16, the CILI 7-minute peg). This no longer
--    describes the native router: it embeds type_id as a plan literal, and PG18
--    prunes to the owning LIST partition before the matched/unmatched join.
--  * per-type loop re-unnesting the FULL arrays each iteration: O(2·N·T)
--    materializations (21s insert / 60s re-fold at N=200k,T=10).
--  * BATCH-ONCE temp table (2026-07-16): correct and O(N) — but still a fresh
--    CREATE TEMP TABLE + CREATE INDEX + ANALYZE on every call, and generic
--    per-type statements re-planned per call.
--
-- The native routing groups the batch by type in C and executes one SESSION-CACHED
-- MERGE plan per type whose type_id is a LITERAL in the plan text (HTAB of type ->
-- SPI_keepplan'd plan in TopMemoryContext): LIST pruning once per (backend, type),
-- matched/unmatched decided in one target join, HASH pruning per row, no temp table,
-- no ANALYZE, no re-plan, and no UPDATE-then-NOT-EXISTS double probe.
--
-- One implementation per fact, preserved:
--  * the Glicko fold runs the SAME core (glicko2_init + glicko2_fold_uniform_period)
--    the scalar laplace_glicko2_accumulate_games wraps — computed in one native
--    pass per type run for BOTH arms: matched cells fold from their stored prior
--    (read and row-locked by a per-type FOR UPDATE probe), novel cells from the
--    neutral prior; the rating period IS the batch. The scalar remains in the
--    MERGE only as the lazy MATCHED fallback for a cell inserted concurrently
--    between the prior read and the MERGE;
--  * cell ids are computed in C through the SAME core hash the SQL
--    laplace.consensus_id() wraps — blake3(subject || type || COALESCE(object, 16 zero
--    bytes)) — byte-identical layout;
--  * the duplicate-cell contract check raises the same cardinality_violation.
--
-- NO mask queue here: the caller deposits highway bits INLINE for this same
-- delta (consensus.highway_mask_deposit); highway_mask_dirty is populated only by the
-- repair verbs, which need to CLEAR bits (per-source evict) — something an
-- OR-accumulate deposit cannot express.
--
-- Contract with the caller (ConsensusAccumulatingWriter) — unchanged:
--   * arrays are parallel and CLIENT-DEDUPED per call — one row per
--     (subject, type, object) cell;
--   * phi is uniform per cell per call (the writer's merge invariant);
--   * rows arrive sorted by (type, subject, id) — partition-key order; the
--     router only needs same-type rows ADJACENT and remains correct (merely
--     one extra plan execution) if they are not.
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS laplace.consensus_upsert(bytea[], bytea[], bytea[], bigint[], bigint[], bigint[], timestamptz[]);
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION consensus.upsert(
    p_subjects bytea[],
    p_types    bytea[],
    p_objects  bytea[],
    p_phis     bigint[],
    p_games    bigint[],
    p_sums     bigint[],
    p_ts       timestamptz[])
    RETURNS bigint
    AS 'MODULE_PATHNAME', 'pg_laplace_consensus_upsert'
    LANGUAGE C VOLATILE;

-- Direct routed form for first-party type lanes. The type is part of every cell
-- identity but is transmitted once per set operation, not once per row.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION consensus.upsert_type(
    p_type     bytea,
    p_subjects bytea[],
    p_objects  bytea[],
    p_phis     bigint[],
    p_games    bigint[],
    p_sums     bigint[],
    p_ts       timestamptz[])
    RETURNS bigint
    AS 'MODULE_PATHNAME', 'pg_laplace_consensus_upsert_type'
    LANGUAGE C VOLATILE;
